 "about_text": "Nüart Gallery was established in Santa Fe at the start of the 21st century and has grown into a 3,000-square-foot, ten-room space on Canyon Road showing contemporary abstract and figurative art. Over more than two decades it has mounted upwards of 250 solo and group exhibitions, introducing many artists to the U.S. market and shipping worldwide. In 2023 the gallery expanded with a second 3,000-square-foot location at Bergamot Station in Santa Monica, extending its reach into the Los Angeles market. The program represents around 40 artists working locally and internationally, with works held in major museum collections such as MoMA, LACMA, the Getty, and the Tate Modern. The gallery also carries limited inventory from blue-chip artists.",
